From d18b4af8eb093e5695302858365151dcf1ce98f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:01:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/78] Port UI_RequestChoice and the Play/Demo prompt

Ports H008+$01FC UI_RequestChoice with its nested procedures ($01A0,
$020A, $03C8): option parsing, highlighted drawing on row 24, keys
(letters, Enter, Esc, 4/6 to move, digit mapping, Alt shortcuts), mouse
clicks on the option row and the game areas, pointer shape updates,
picture-set animation and the prompt timeout. The parent's locals,
reached through its frame by the nested procedures, become a struct.
Also ports H029+$01B6 (pointer shape), H029+$03E2, H030+$00B6 and
H030+$0A40, and ModifyIDCMP. The H001 call used the wrong argument
order; it now follows the push order.

The prompt shows 'Champions of Krynn v1.0 Play Demo', times out to Demo
after 30 seconds, and P or Right+Enter choose Play or Demo. On the
host, COK_KEYS injects timed key presses for tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013G8KST8dgGfenpqx3RukYi
